.TH CHOWN 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
chown \- change file owner and group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chown
[\fB\-R\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] \fIOWNER\fR[\fB:\fR\fIGROUP\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the owner (and optionally group, via \fBOWNER:GROUP\fR) of each FILE. Owner/group are resolved by name via the host's passwd/group database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-R, \-\-recursive
Change files and directories recursively.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
With \fB\-R\fR on Linux, traversal is TOCTOU-hardened (common::safewalk). A numeric uid:gid without a matching passwd/group entry is not supported.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a general failure (a listed file could not be processed, etc.), 2 on a usage error (missing or invalid arguments).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
